<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sebastián Hurtado de Corcuera</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1587–1660</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sebastián Hurtado de Corcuera was a Spanish soldier and governor-general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> from 1635 to 1644. He led campaigns against the Muslim sultanates of the south, capturing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan-kudarat">Sultan Kudarat</a>'s stronghold at Lamitan in 1637 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jolo">Jolo</a> in 1638. His quarrels with the Archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> and the loss of the Spanish post on Formosa to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> in 1642 led to his imprisonment after his term.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sebastian-hurtado-de-corcuera.jpg" alt="Sebastián Hurtado de Corcuera" width="226" height="293" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sebasti%C3%A1n_Hurtado_de_Corcuera.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
